                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/196: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-22T16:00:00+08:00">August 22, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 22—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>489. Department’s 166, August 20, 2 p.m. The following telegraphic instruction
                    has been sent to Tsinanfu August 25, noon: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The following instructions are intended specifically for Tsinanfu. You
                            should send a final warning to all American citizens in your district,
                            advising them to proceed at once to Tsingtao or such other place of
                            concentration as you may consider easiest and safest and stating that
                            your office will shortly be closed. When you feel that you have done
                            everything reasonably possible to effect withdrawal of Americans in your
                            district, you should close your office, turning custody thereof over to
                            Chinese authorities, and proceed to Tsingtao, with those members of your
                            Chinese staff who wish to accompany you to that place.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
